-- coa7-ch3c.l4: Part 13 Chapter 3, Resolutions at meetings: members' statements and procedure at meetings
-- (ss 314 to 323), lines 4059-4142 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- Tag conventions are those of coa7-ch1.l4. Seam taken as an input: `s 1121 the officer is in default` (coa24).

§§ `Members' statements`

-- ---- s 314 Members' power to require circulation of statements --------------------------------------------

-- src:4061 | (1) The members of a company may require the company to circulate, to members of the company entitled to receive notice of a general meeting, a statement of not more than 1,000 words with respect to—
-- src:4062 | (a) a matter referred to in a proposed resolution to be dealt with at that meeting, or
-- src:4063 | (b) other business to be dealt with at that meeting.
@ref s 314(1) Members' power to require circulation of statements (src:4061-4063)
GIVEN `words in the statement` IS A NUMBER
      `the statement is with respect to a matter referred to in a proposed resolution to be dealt with at the meeting, or to other business to be dealt with at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 314(1) the members may require the company to circulate the statement` MEANS
    IF `words in the statement` AT MOST 1000 AND `the statement is with respect to a matter referred to in a proposed resolution to be dealt with at the meeting, or to other business to be dealt with at the meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a statement of not more than 1,000 words with respect to— (a) a matter referred to in a proposed resolution to be dealt with at that meeting, or (b) other business to be dealt with at that meeting"

DECLARE `s 314(3) kind of statement` IS ONE OF
    `s 314(3)(a) a statement with respect to a matter referred to in a proposed resolution`
    `s 314(3)(b) any other statement`

-- src:4068 | (3) In subsection (2), a “relevant right to vote” means—
-- src:4069 | (a) in relation to a statement with respect to a matter referred to in a proposed resolution, a right to vote on that resolution at the meeting to which the requests relate, and
-- src:4070 | (b) in relation to any other statement, a right to vote at the meeting to which the requests relate.
@ref s 314(3) Members' power to require circulation of statements: "relevant right to vote" (src:4068-4070)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 314(3) kind of statement`
      `the member has a right to vote on that resolution at the meeting to which the requests relate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member has a right to vote at the meeting to which the requests relate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 314(3) the member has a relevant right to vote` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 314(3)(a) a statement with respect to a matter referred to in a proposed resolution` THEN
        IF `the member has a right to vote on that resolution at the meeting to which the requests relate`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a “relevant right to vote” means— (a) in relation to a statement with respect to a matter referred to in a proposed resolution, a right to vote on that resolution at the meeting to which the requests relate"
    WHEN `s 314(3)(b) any other statement` THEN
        IF `the member has a right to vote at the meeting to which the requests relate`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in relation to any other statement, a right to vote at the meeting to which the requests relate"

-- (a) members representing at least 5% of the total voting rights of the members with a relevant right to vote (treasury
-- shares excluded), or (b) at least 100 such members holding shares on which an average of at least £100 per member is paid up.
-- src:4064 | (2) A company is required to circulate a statement once it has received requests to do so from—
-- src:4065 | (a) members representing at least 5% of the total voting rights of all the members who have a relevant right to vote (excluding any voting rights attached to any shares in the company held as treasury shares), or
-- src:4066 | (b) at least 100 members who have a relevant right to vote and hold shares in the company on which there has been paid up an average sum, per member, of at least £100.
-- src:4067 | See also section 153 (exercise of rights where shares held on behalf of others).
@ref s 314(2) Members' power to require circulation of statements: the requests (src:4064-4067)
GIVEN `voting rights represented by the requesting members who have a relevant right to vote` IS A NUMBER
      `total voting rights of all the members who have a relevant right to vote (excluding voting rights attached to treasury shares)` IS A NUMBER
      `number of requesting members who have a relevant right to vote and hold shares in the company` IS A NUMBER
      `total sum paid up on the shares those members hold` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 314(2) the company is required to circulate the statement` MEANS
    IF `voting rights represented by the requesting members who have a relevant right to vote` TIMES 20 AT LEAST `total voting rights of all the members who have a relevant right to vote (excluding voting rights attached to treasury shares)`
        OR (`number of requesting members who have a relevant right to vote and hold shares in the company` AT LEAST 100
            AND `total sum paid up on the shares those members hold` AT LEAST `number of requesting members who have a relevant right to vote and hold shares in the company` TIMES 100)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company is required to circulate a statement once it has received requests to do so from— (a) members representing at least 5% of the total voting rights ... or (b) at least 100 members" -- MARGINAL a

-- src:4071 | (4) A request—
-- src:4072 | (a) may be in hard copy form or in electronic form,
-- src:4073 | (b) must identify the statement to be circulated,
-- src:4074 | (c) must be authenticated by the person or persons making it, and
-- src:4075 | (d) must be received by the company at least one week before the meeting to which it relates.
@ref s 314(4) Members' power to require circulation of statements: the request (src:4071-4075)
GIVEN `the request is in hard copy form or in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request identifies the statement to be circulated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is authenticated by the person or persons making it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the company received the request` IS A DATE
      `the day of the meeting to which the request relates` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 314(4) the request meets the requirements of this subsection` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the request is in hard copy form or in electronic form`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A request— (a) may be in hard copy form or in electronic form"
    ELSE IF `the request identifies the statement to be circulated`
            AND `the request is authenticated by the person or persons making it`
            AND `s 360(2) the period of the specified length is satisfied` 7 `the day on which the company received the request` `the day of the meeting to which the request relates` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) must identify the statement to be circulated, (c) must be authenticated by the person or persons making it, and (d) must be received by the company at least one week before the meeting to which it relates" -- FORK F5

-- ---- s 315 Company's duty to circulate members' statement -------------------------------------------------

-- src:4077 | (1) A company that is required under section 314, to circulate a statement must send a copy of it to each member of the company entitled to receive notice of the meeting—
@ref s 315(1) Company's duty to circulate members' statement (src:4077)
GIVEN `the company is required under section 314 to circulate the statement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 315(1) the company must send a copy of the statement to each member entitled to receive notice of the meeting` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the company is required under section 314 to circulate the statement`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company that is required under section 314, to circulate a statement must send a copy of it" -- MARGINAL a
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 314 requires the circulation is not known

-- src:4078 | (a) in the same manner as the notice of the meeting, and
@ref s 315(1)(a) Company's duty to circulate members' statement: the manner (src:4078)
GIVEN `the copy is sent in the same manner as the notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 315(1)(a) the copy was sent in the manner this paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF `the copy is sent in the same manner as the notice of the meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must send a copy of it to each member of the company entitled to receive notice of the meeting— (a) in the same manner as the notice of the meeting" -- FORK F5

-- src:4079 | (b) at the same time as, or as soon as reasonably practicable after, it gives notice of the meeting.
@ref s 315(1)(b) Company's duty to circulate members' statement: the time (src:4079)
GIVEN `the copy is sent at the same time as, or as soon as reasonably practicable after, the company gives notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 315(1)(b) the copy was sent at a time this paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF `the copy is sent at the same time as, or as soon as reasonably practicable after, the company gives notice of the meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) at the same time as, or as soon as reasonably practicable after, it gives notice of the meeting" -- FORK F5

-- src:4080 | (2) Subsection (1) has effect subject to section 316(2) (deposit or tender of sum in respect of expenses of circulation) and section 317 (application not to circulate members' statement).
@ref s 315(2) Company's duty to circulate members' statement: subject to ss 316(2) and 317 (src:4080)
GIVEN `s 316(2) the company is bound to comply with section 315` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 317(1) the company is not required to circulate the members' statement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 315(2) subsection (1) has effect` MEANS
    IF `s 316(2) the company is bound to comply with section 315` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) has effect subject to section 316(2) (deposit or tender of sum in respect of expenses of circulation)" -- FORK F4
    ELSE IF `s 317(1) the company is not required to circulate the members' statement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and section 317 (application not to circulate members' statement)" -- FORK F4
         ELSE IF `s 316(2) the company is bound to comply with section 315` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 317(1) the company is not required to circulate the members' statement` EQUALS JUST FALSE
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answers of section 316(2) or section 317(1) are not known

-- src:4081 | (3) In the event of default in complying with this section, an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 315(3) Company's duty to circulate members' statement: offence (src:4081)
GIVEN `the company is in default in complying with this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 315(3) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the company is in default in complying with this section`
    THEN `s 1121 the officer is in default`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the event of default in complying with this section, an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default." -- MARGINAL a
-- src:4082 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:4083 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:4084 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 315(4) Company's duty to circulate members' statement: penalty (src:4082-4084)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 315(4) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), NOTHING, FALSE)

-- ---- s 316 Expenses of circulating members' statement ----------------------------------------------------

-- src:4086 | (1) The expenses of the company in complying with section 315 need not be paid by the members who requested the circulation of the statement if—
-- src:4087 | (a) the meeting to which the requests relate is an annual general meeting of a public company, and
-- src:4088 | (b) requests sufficient to require the company to circulate the statement are received before the end of the financial year preceding the meeting.
@ref s 316(1) Expenses of circulating members' statement: expenses need not be paid (src:4086-4088)
GIVEN `the meeting to which the requests relate is an annual general meeting of a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which requests sufficient to require the company to circulate the statement were received` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the financial year preceding the meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 316(1) the expenses need not be paid by the members who requested the circulation` MEANS
    IF `the meeting to which the requests relate is an annual general meeting of a public company`
        AND `the day on which requests sufficient to require the company to circulate the statement were received` AT MOST `the last day of the financial year preceding the meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "need not be paid by the members who requested the circulation of the statement if— (a) the meeting to which the requests relate is an annual general meeting of a public company, and (b) requests sufficient to require the company to circulate the statement are received before the end of the financial year preceding the meeting" -- MARGINAL a -- FORK F20

-- src:4090 | (a) the expenses of the company in complying with that section must be paid by the members who requested the circulation of the statement unless the company resolves otherwise, and
@ref s 316(2)(a) Expenses of circulating members' statement: otherwise, the members pay (src:4090)
GIVEN `subsection (1) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has resolved otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 316(2)(a) the expenses must be paid by the members who requested the circulation` MEANS
    IF `subsection (1) applies`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Otherwise—" -- FORK F21
    ELSE IF `the company has resolved otherwise`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be paid by the members who requested the circulation of the statement unless the company resolves otherwise"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:4091 | (b) unless the company has previously so resolved, it is not bound to comply with that section unless there is deposited with or tendered to it, not later than one week before the meeting, a sum reasonably sufficient to meet its expenses in doing so.
@ref s 316(2)(b) Expenses of circulating members' statement: deposit or tender (src:4091)
GIVEN `subsection (1) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has previously resolved to meet the expenses` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a sum reasonably sufficient to meet the company's expenses was deposited with or tendered to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the sum was deposited or tendered` IS A DATE
      `the day of the meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 316(2) the company is bound to comply with section 315` MEANS
    IF `subsection (1) applies`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Otherwise—" -- FORK F21
    ELSE IF `the company has previously resolved to meet the expenses`
         THEN JUST TRUE -- FORK F6
         ELSE IF `a sum reasonably sufficient to meet the company's expenses was deposited with or tendered to it`
                 AND `s 360(2) the period of the specified length is satisfied` 7 `the day on which the sum was deposited or tendered` `the day of the meeting` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              THEN JUST TRUE -- FORK F6
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is not bound to comply with that section unless there is deposited with or tendered to it, not later than one week before the meeting, a sum reasonably sufficient to meet its expenses in doing so"

-- ---- s 317 Application not to circulate members' statement ------------------------------------------------

-- src:4093 | (1) A company is not required to circulate a members' statement under section 315 if, on an application by the company or another person who claims to be aggrieved, the court is satisfied that the rights conferred by section 314 and that section are being abused.
@ref s 317(1) Application not to circulate members' statement (src:4093)
GIVEN `an application was made by the company or by another person who claims to be aggrieved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the rights conferred by sections 314 and 315 are being abused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 317(1) the company is not required to circulate the members' statement` MEANS
    IF `an application was made by the company or by another person who claims to be aggrieved`
        AND `the court is satisfied that the rights conferred by sections 314 and 315 are being abused`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not required to circulate a members' statement under section 315 if, on an application by the company or another person who claims to be aggrieved, the court is satisfied that the rights conferred by section 314 and that section are being abused" -- MARGINAL a

-- src:4094 | (2) The court may order the members who requested the circulation of the statement to pay the whole or part of the company's costs (in Scotland, expenses) on such an application, even if they are not parties to the application.
@ref s 317(2) Application not to circulate members' statement: costs (src:4094)
GIVEN `an application was made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 317(2) the court may order the members who requested the circulation to pay the company's costs` MEANS
    IF `an application was made under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on such an application, even if they are not parties to the application"

§§ `Procedure at meetings`

-- ---- s 318 Quorum at meetings ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- A person present at a meeting, with the capacities in which the person is a qualifying person (s 318(3)): an individual
-- who is a member; authorised under s 323 as the representative of a corporation (the corporation's identity is given);
-- appointed as proxy of a member (the member's identity is given).
DECLARE `s 318 person present` HAS
    `identity of the person present` IS A STRING
    `an individual who is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `authorised under section 323 to act as the representative of this corporation` IS A MAYBE STRING
    `appointed as proxy of this member` IS A MAYBE STRING

-- src:4097 | (1) In the case of a company limited by shares or guarantee and having only one member, one qualifying person present at a meeting is a quorum.
@ref s 318(1) Quorum at meetings: a company with one member (src:4097)
GIVEN `the company is limited by shares or guarantee and has only one member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the persons present` IS A LIST OF `s 318 person present`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 318(1) one qualifying person present is a quorum` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is limited by shares or guarantee and has only one member`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a company limited by shares or guarantee and having only one member"
    ELSE IF any (GIVEN person YIELD `s 318(3) the person is a qualifying person` person EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the persons present`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no qualifying person is present, and the subsection says only that one is a quorum

-- The corporation whose representative the person is, where that is the only reason the person is a qualifying person.
-- src:4098 | (2) In any other case, subject to the provisions of the company's articles, two qualifying persons present at a meeting are a quorum, unless—
-- src:4099 | (a) each is a qualifying person only because he is authorised under section 323 to act as the representative of a corporation in relation to the meeting, and they are representatives of the same corporation; or
-- src:4100 | (b) each is a qualifying person only because he is appointed as proxy of a member in relation to the meeting, and they are proxies of the same member.
@ref s 318(2)(a) Quorum at meetings: a qualifying person only as a corporation's representative (src:4098-4100)
GIVEN person IS A `s 318 person present`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 318(2)(a) the corporation whose representative the person is, the person being a qualifying person only for that reason` MEANS
    IF person's `an individual who is a member of the company`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "each is a qualifying person only because he is authorised under section 323"
    ELSE IF isJust (person's `appointed as proxy of this member`)
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "each is a qualifying person only because he is authorised under section 323"
         ELSE person's `authorised under section 323 to act as the representative of this corporation`

@ref s 318(2)(b) Quorum at meetings: a qualifying person only as a member's proxy (src:4100)
GIVEN person IS A `s 318 person present`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 318(2)(b) the member whose proxy the person is, the person being a qualifying person only for that reason` MEANS
    IF person's `an individual who is a member of the company`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "each is a qualifying person only because he is appointed as proxy of a member"
    ELSE IF isJust (person's `authorised under section 323 to act as the representative of this corporation`)
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "each is a qualifying person only because he is appointed as proxy of a member"
         ELSE person's `appointed as proxy of this member`

-- Two distinct persons are a quorum unless (a) each is a qualifying person only as representative of the same corporation or
-- (b) each is a qualifying person only as proxy of the same member.
@ref s 318(2) Quorum at meetings: two persons (src:4098-4100)
GIVEN first IS A `s 318 person present`
      second IS A `s 318 person present`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 318(2) these two persons present are a quorum` MEANS
    IF first's `identity of the person present` EQUALS second's `identity of the person present`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "two qualifying persons present are a quorum": one person is not two
    ELSE IF `s 318(3) the person is a qualifying person` first EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `s 318(3) the person is a qualifying person` second EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "two qualifying persons present are a quorum"
         ELSE IF (isJust (`s 318(2)(a) the corporation whose representative the person is, the person being a qualifying person only for that reason` first)
                  AND `s 318(2)(a) the corporation whose representative the person is, the person being a qualifying person only for that reason` first EQUALS `s 318(2)(a) the corporation whose representative the person is, the person being a qualifying person only for that reason` second)
                 OR (isJust (`s 318(2)(b) the member whose proxy the person is, the person being a qualifying person only for that reason` first)
                  AND `s 318(2)(b) the member whose proxy the person is, the person being a qualifying person only for that reason` first EQUALS `s 318(2)(b) the member whose proxy the person is, the person being a qualifying person only for that reason` second)
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "two qualifying persons present are a quorum, unless— (a) each is a qualifying person only because he is authorised under section 323 ... and they are representatives of the same corporation; or (b) ... proxies of the same member"
              ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 318(2) Quorum at meetings: in any other case (src:4098-4100)
GIVEN `the company's articles provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the persons present` IS A LIST OF `s 318 person present`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 318(2) two qualifying persons present are a quorum` MEANS
    IF `the company's articles provide otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subject to the provisions of the company's articles"
    ELSE IF any (GIVEN first YIELD any (GIVEN second YIELD `s 318(2) these two persons present are a quorum` first second EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the persons present`) `the persons present`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In any other case, subject to the provisions of the company's articles, two qualifying persons present at a meeting are a quorum" -- FORK F13

-- src:4101 | (3) For the purposes of this section a “qualifying person” means—
-- src:4102 | (a) an individual who is a member of the company,
-- src:4103 | (b) a person authorised under section 323 (representation of corporations at meetings) to act as the representative of a corporation in relation to the meeting, or
-- src:4104 | (c) a person appointed as proxy of a member in relation to the meeting.
@ref s 318(3) Quorum at meetings: "qualifying person" (src:4101-4104)
GIVEN person IS A `s 318 person present`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 318(3) the person is a qualifying person` MEANS
    IF person's `an individual who is a member of the company`
        OR isJust (person's `authorised under section 323 to act as the representative of this corporation`)
        OR isJust (person's `appointed as proxy of this member`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a “qualifying person” means— (a) an individual who is a member of the company, (b) a person authorised under section 323 ... or (c) a person appointed as proxy of a member"

-- ---- s 319 Chairman of meeting ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4106 | (1) A member may be elected to be the chairman of a general meeting by a resolution of the company passed at the meeting.
-- src:4107 | (2) Subsection (1) is subject to any provision of the company's articles that states who may or may not be chairman.
@ref s 319 Chairman of meeting (src:4106-4107)
GIVEN `the person is a member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is elected chairman of the general meeting by a resolution of the company passed at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's articles state who may or may not be chairman` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 319(1) the member may be elected chairman of the general meeting` MEANS
    IF `the company's articles state who may or may not be chairman`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subsection (1) is subject to any provision of the company's articles that states who may or may not be chairman"
    ELSE IF `the person is a member` AND `the person is elected chairman of the general meeting by a resolution of the company passed at the meeting`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A member may be elected to be the chairman of a general meeting by a resolution of the company passed at the meeting"

-- ---- s 319A Traded companies: questions at meetings ------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4110 | (2) No such answer need be given—
-- src:4111 | (a) if to do so would—
-- src:4112 | (i) interfere unduly with the preparation for the meeting, or
-- src:4113 | (ii) involve the disclosure of confidential information;
-- src:4114 | (b) if the answer has already been given on a website in the form of an answer to a question; or
-- src:4115 | (c) if it is undesirable in the interests of the company or the good order of the meeting that the question be answered.
@ref s 319A(2) Traded companies: questions at meetings: no answer need be given (src:4110-4115)
GIVEN `to answer would interfere unduly with the preparation for the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `to answer would involve the disclosure of confidential information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer has already been given on a website in the form of an answer to a question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is undesirable in the interests of the company or the good order of the meeting that the question be answered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 319A(2) no answer need be given` MEANS
    IF `to answer would interfere unduly with the preparation for the meeting`
        OR `to answer would involve the disclosure of confidential information`
        OR `the answer has already been given on a website in the form of an answer to a question`
        OR `it is undesirable in the interests of the company or the good order of the meeting that the question be answered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No such answer need be given— (a) if to do so would— ... (b) if the answer has already been given on a website ...; or (c) if it is undesirable in the interests of the company or the good order of the meeting" -- MARGINAL a

-- src:4109 | (1) At a general meeting of a traded company, the company must cause to be answered any question relating to the business being dealt with at the meeting put by a member attending the meeting.
@ref s 319A(1) Traded companies: questions at meetings (src:4109)
GIVEN `the company is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question relates to the business being dealt with at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question is put by a member attending the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 319A(2) no answer need be given` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 319A(1) the company must cause the question to be answered` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a traded company`) OR (NOT `the question relates to the business being dealt with at the meeting`) OR (NOT `the question is put by a member attending the meeting`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "At a general meeting of a traded company, the company must cause to be answered any question relating to the business being dealt with at the meeting put by a member attending the meeting"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 319A(2) no answer need be given`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No such answer need be given" -- FORK F14
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether an exception of subsection (2) applies is not known

-- ---- s 320 Declaration by chairman on a show of hands ----------------------------------------------------

-- src:4122 | (3) This section does not have effect if a poll is demanded in respect of the resolution (and the demand is not subsequently withdrawn).
@ref s 320(3) Declaration by chairman on a show of hands: where a poll is demanded (src:4122)
GIVEN `a poll is demanded in respect of the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the demand is subsequently withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320(3) this section has effect` MEANS
    IF `a poll is demanded in respect of the resolution` AND (NOT `the demand is subsequently withdrawn`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not have effect if a poll is demanded in respect of the resolution (and the demand is not subsequently withdrawn)"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:4117 | (1) On a vote on a resolution at a meeting on a show of hands, a declaration by the chairman that the resolution—
-- src:4118 | (a) has or has not been passed, or
-- src:4119 | (b) passed with a particular majority,
-- src:4120 | is conclusive evidence of that fact without proof of the number or proportion of the votes recorded in favour of or against the resolution.
@ref s 320(1) Declaration by chairman on a show of hands (src:4117-4120)
GIVEN `the vote was on a show of hands at a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the chairman declared that the resolution has or has not been passed, or passed with a particular majority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 320(3) this section has effect` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320(1) the declaration is conclusive evidence of that fact without proof of the number or proportion of the votes` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the vote was on a show of hands at a meeting`) OR (NOT `the chairman declared that the resolution has or has not been passed, or passed with a particular majority`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On a vote on a resolution at a meeting on a show of hands, a declaration by the chairman"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 320(3) this section has effect`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not have effect if a poll is demanded" -- FORK F4
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section has effect is not known

-- src:4121 | (2) An entry in respect of such a declaration in minutes of the meeting recorded in accordance with section 355 is also conclusive evidence of that fact without such proof.
@ref s 320(2) Declaration by chairman on a show of hands: the minutes (src:4121)
GIVEN `the declaration is entered in minutes of the meeting recorded in accordance with section 355` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 320(3) this section has effect` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320(2) the entry in the minutes is conclusive evidence of that fact without proof` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the declaration is entered in minutes of the meeting recorded in accordance with section 355`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An entry in respect of such a declaration in minutes of the meeting recorded in accordance with section 355"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 320(3) this section has effect`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not have effect if a poll is demanded" -- FORK F4
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section has effect is not known

-- ---- s 321 Right to demand a poll -------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 321 question` IS ONE OF
    `s 321(1)(a) the election of the chairman of the meeting`
    `s 321(1)(b) the adjournment of the meeting`
    `s 321 any other question`

-- src:4124 | (1) A provision of a company's articles is void in so far as it would have the effect of excluding the right to demand a poll at a general meeting on any question other than—
-- src:4125 | (a) the election of the chairman of the meeting, or
-- src:4126 | (b) the adjournment of the meeting.
@ref s 321(1) Right to demand a poll: a provision excluding the right (src:4124-4126)
GIVEN question IS A `s 321 question`
      `the provision of the articles has the effect of excluding the right to demand a poll at a general meeting on the question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 321(1) the provision of the articles is void` MEANS
    CONSIDER question
    WHEN `s 321 any other question` THEN
        IF `the provision of the articles has the effect of excluding the right to demand a poll at a general meeting on the question`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is void in so far as it would have the effect of excluding the right to demand a poll"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on any question other than— (a) the election of the chairman of the meeting, or (b) the adjournment of the meeting" -- FORK F19

-- (2): a demand made by (a) not less than 5 members with the right to vote, (b) members representing not less than 10% of the
-- voting rights (treasury shares excluded), or (c) members holding shares with not less than 10% of the sum paid up on all
-- the voting shares (treasury shares excluded), on any question other than (1)(a) and (b).
-- src:4127 | (2) A provision of a company's articles is void in so far as it would have the effect of making ineffective a demand for a poll on any such question which is made—
-- src:4128 | (a) by not less than 5 members having the right to vote on the resolution; or
-- src:4129 | (b) by a member or members representing not less than 10% of the total voting rights of all the members having the right to vote on the resolution (excluding any voting rights attached to any shares in the company held as treasury shares); or
-- src:4130 | (c) by a member or members holding shares in the company conferring a right to vote on the resolution, being shares on which an aggregate sum has been paid up equal to not less than 10% of the total sum paid up on all the shares conferring that right (excluding shares in the company conferring a right to vote on the resolution which are held as treasury shares).
@ref s 321(2) Right to demand a poll: a provision making a demand ineffective (src:4127-4130)
GIVEN question IS A `s 321 question`
      `members with the right to vote on the resolution who make the demand` IS A NUMBER
      `voting rights represented by the members who make the demand` IS A NUMBER
      `total voting rights of all the members having the right to vote on the resolution (excluding treasury shares)` IS A NUMBER
      `sum paid up on the shares held by the members who make the demand` IS A NUMBER
      `total sum paid up on all the shares conferring the right to vote on the resolution (excluding treasury shares)` IS A NUMBER
      `the provision of the articles has the effect of making the demand ineffective` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 321(2) the provision of the articles is void` MEANS
    CONSIDER question
    WHEN `s 321 any other question` THEN
        IF `the provision of the articles has the effect of making the demand ineffective`
            AND (`members with the right to vote on the resolution who make the demand` AT LEAST 5
                 OR `voting rights represented by the members who make the demand` TIMES 10 AT LEAST `total voting rights of all the members having the right to vote on the resolution (excluding treasury shares)`
                 OR `sum paid up on the shares held by the members who make the demand` TIMES 10 AT LEAST `total sum paid up on all the shares conferring the right to vote on the resolution (excluding treasury shares)`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is void in so far as it would have the effect of making ineffective a demand for a poll on any such question which is made— (a) ... (b) ... or (c) ..."
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any such question"

-- ---- s 322 Voting on a poll -------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4132 | On a poll taken at a general meeting of a company, a member entitled to more than one vote need not, if he votes, use all his votes or cast all the votes he uses in the same way.
@ref s 322 Voting on a poll (src:4132)
GIVEN `votes the member is entitled to on the poll` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 322 the member need not use all his votes or cast all the votes he uses in the same way` MEANS
    IF `votes the member is entitled to on the poll` GREATER THAN 1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a member entitled to more than one vote"

-- ---- s 322A Voting on a poll: votes cast in advance -------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4134 | (1) A company's articles may contain provision to the effect that on a vote on a resolution on a poll taken at a meeting, the votes may include votes cast in advance.
@ref s 322A(1) Voting on a poll: votes cast in advance (src:4134)
GIVEN `the company's articles contain provision that on a vote on a resolution on a poll taken at a meeting the votes may include votes cast in advance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 322A(1) the votes on the poll include votes cast in advance` MEANS
    IF `the company's articles contain provision that on a vote on a resolution on a poll taken at a meeting the votes may include votes cast in advance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company's articles may contain provision to the effect that"

-- src:4135 | (2) In the case of a traded company any such provision in relation to voting at a general meeting may be made subject only to such requirements and restrictions as are—
-- src:4136 | (a) necessary to ensure the identification of the person voting, and
-- src:4137 | (b) proportionate to the achievement of that objective.
@ref s 322A(2) Voting on a poll: votes cast in advance: traded companies (src:4135-4137)
GIVEN `the company is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement or restriction is necessary to ensure the identification of the person voting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement or restriction is proportionate to the achievement of that objective` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 322A(2) the provision may be made subject to the requirement or restriction` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a traded company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a traded company"
    ELSE IF `the requirement or restriction is necessary to ensure the identification of the person voting` AND `the requirement or restriction is proportionate to the achievement of that objective`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be made subject only to such requirements and restrictions as are— (a) necessary to ensure the identification of the person voting, and (b) proportionate to the achievement of that objective" -- FORK F11

-- src:4138 | Nothing in this subsection affects any power of a company to require reasonable evidence of the entitlement of any person who is not a member to vote.
@ref s 322A(2) Voting on a poll: votes cast in advance: evidence of entitlement (src:4138)
GIVEN `the person is not a member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 322A(2) the company may require reasonable evidence of the entitlement of the person to vote` MEANS
    IF `the person is not a member`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person who is not a member"

-- "No account is to be taken of any part of a day that is not a working day": the hours that count.
-- src:4142 | (4) In calculating the periods mentioned in subsection (3), no account is to be taken of any part of a day that is not a working day.
@ref s 322A(4) Voting on a poll: votes cast in advance: calculating the periods (src:4142)
GIVEN `hours in the period` IS A NUMBER
      `hours of the period that fall on a day that is not a working day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 322A(4) the hours of the period that are counted` MEANS
    `hours in the period` MINUS `hours of the period that fall on a day that is not a working day`

-- src:4139 | (3) Any provision of a company's articles is void in so far as it would have the effect of requiring any document casting a vote in advance to be received by the company or another person earlier than the following time—
-- src:4140 | (a) in the case of a poll taken more than 48 hours after it was demanded, 24 hours before the time appointed for the taking of the poll;
-- src:4141 | (b) in the case of any other poll, 48 hours before the time for holding the meeting or adjourned meeting.
@ref s 322A(3) Voting on a poll: votes cast in advance: the latest time the articles may require (src:4139-4141)
GIVEN `the poll is taken more than 48 hours after it was demanded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `hours before the relevant time that the articles require the document casting the vote to be received` IS A NUMBER
      `of those hours, the hours that fall on a day that is not a working day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 322A(3) the provision of the articles is void` MEANS
    IF `s 322A(4) the hours of the period that are counted` `hours before the relevant time that the articles require the document casting the vote to be received` `of those hours, the hours that fall on a day that is not a working day`
         GREATER THAN (IF `the poll is taken more than 48 hours after it was demanded` THEN 24 ELSE 48)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is void in so far as it would have the effect of requiring any document casting a vote in advance to be received by the company or another person earlier than the following time"

-- ---- s 323 Representation of corporations at meetings -----------------------------------------------------

-- src:4144 | (1) If a corporation (whether or not a company within the meaning of this Act) is a member of a company, it may by resolution of its directors or other governing body authorise a person or persons to act as its representative or representatives at any meeting of the company.
@ref s 323(1) Representation of corporations at meetings (src:4144)
GIVEN `the corporation is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is authorised by resolution of the corporation's directors or other governing body to act as its representative at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 323(1) the person is authorised to act as the corporation's representative` MEANS
    IF `the corporation is a member of the company` AND `the person is authorised by resolution of the corporation's directors or other governing body to act as its representative at the meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a corporation ... is a member of a company, it may by resolution of its directors or other governing body authorise a person or persons to act as its representative or representatives at any meeting of the company"

-- src:4145 | (2) A person authorised by a corporation is entitled to exercise (on behalf of the corporation) the same powers as the corporation could exercise if it were an individual member of the company. Where a corporation authorises more than one person, this subsection is subject to subsections (3) and (4).
@ref s 323(2) Representation of corporations at meetings: the powers (src:4145)
GIVEN `the person is authorised by a corporation under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 323(2) the person is entitled to exercise the same powers on behalf of the corporation as an individual member could` MEANS
    IF `the person is authorised by a corporation under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person authorised by a corporation is entitled to exercise (on behalf of the corporation) the same powers as the corporation could exercise if it were an individual member of the company"

-- src:4146 | (3) On a vote on a resolution on a show of hands at a meeting of the company, each authorised person has the same voting rights as the corporation would be entitled to.
@ref s 323(3) Representation of corporations at meetings: show of hands (src:4146)
GIVEN `the vote is on a resolution on a show of hands at a meeting of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `voting rights the corporation would be entitled to` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 323(3) the voting rights of each authorised person` MEANS
    IF `the vote is on a resolution on a show of hands at a meeting of the company`
    THEN JUST `voting rights the corporation would be entitled to`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On a vote on a resolution on a show of hands at a meeting of the company, each authorised person has the same voting rights as the corporation would be entitled to"

DECLARE `s 323(4) how the power is treated` IS ONE OF
    `s 323(4)(a) as exercised in that way`
    `s 323(4)(b) as not exercised`

-- src:4147 | (4) Where subsection (3) does not apply and more than one authorised person purport to exercise a power under subsection (2) in respect of the same shares—
-- src:4148 | (a) if they purport to exercise the power in the same way as each other, the power is treated as exercised in that way;
-- src:4149 | (b) if they do not purport to exercise the power in the same way as each other, the power is treated as not exercised.
@ref s 323(4) Representation of corporations at meetings: several authorised persons (src:4147-4149)
GIVEN `subsection (3) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `more than one authorised person purport to exercise a power under subsection (2) in respect of the same shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they purport to exercise the power in the same way as each other` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 323(4) how the power is treated`
`s 323(4) the power is treated` MEANS
    IF `subsection (3) applies` OR (NOT `more than one authorised person purport to exercise a power under subsection (2) in respect of the same shares`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where subsection (3) does not apply and more than one authorised person purport to exercise a power under subsection (2) in respect of the same shares"
    ELSE IF `they purport to exercise the power in the same way as each other`
         THEN JUST `s 323(4)(a) as exercised in that way`
         ELSE JUST `s 323(4)(b) as not exercised`
